# Release hygiene — `git archive HEAD` builds the install zip, so every tracked
# path lands in the package unless it is export-ignore'd here. These paths are
# versioned for development/CI/collaboration but are NOT needed to run the
# plugin on a Moodle site, so they are stripped from the release zip.
#
# Three deliberate exceptions to the fleet baseline, the last two upstream artefacts:
#   - tests/ SHIPS in the release (Moodle convention).
#   - LICENSES/ SHIPS: it is upstream's REUSE-style licence text, referenced by
#     README.md, and removing it from the package would break that reference.
#   - CONTRIBUTING.md SHIPS for the same reason — README.md links to it.
#
# LICENSE and COPYING.txt both ship: the plugins directory wants a licence file
# in the package, and MAH's completeness checker wants COPYING.txt by name.
# Every lang pack except en stays in git but not in the zip, upstream's four
# included: the plugins directory accepts only English strings in a package,
# and translations reach sites through AMOS.
#
# Verify with:  git check-attr export-ignore -- <path>
# (a path marked "set" is excluded from the archive; "unspecified" ships).

/.claude              export-ignore
/.DS_Store            export-ignore
/.gitattributes       export-ignore
/.github              export-ignore
/.gitignore           export-ignore
/.moodle-plugin-ci.yml export-ignore
/.phpcsignore         export-ignore
/CLAUDE.md            export-ignore
/docs                 export-ignore
/lang/ca              export-ignore
/lang/es              export-ignore
/lang/eu              export-ignore
/lang/gl              export-ignore
/lang/pt_br           export-ignore
/mutations            export-ignore
/phpcs.xml            export-ignore
